\details{
The offending rows are deliberately not kept in the session afterwards: on
a population register a failed check can hold millions of rows, and they
would stay in memory until the next failure. Messages are shown literally:
braces are not interpolated.
Diagnostic columns such as \code{dupid}, \code{missing}, \code{overlap_id}, \code{gap},
\code{outside} and \code{reason} receive a numeric suffix when their name is already
in the input (for example \code{dupid.1}). All original columns keep their
names and values.

A failed check signals a condition of class \code{inshape_failure} (a warning or
an error) that carries the offending rows in its \code{violations} field.
\code{\link[=violations]{violations()}} catches it and returns the rows, to look at all of them
in the session:

